.TH GSVA 1 2000-1月 "mogsva" "mogsva"
.SH NAME
mogsva \- Run the multi-omics GSVA (moGSVA) analysis on the given multi-omics dataset.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fImogsva(\fBx\fR as <generic> MultiOmicsDataset, 
\fBgeneSet\fR as any, 
\fBopts\fR as <generic> MultiOmicsGsvaOptions, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run the multi-omics GSVA (moGSVA) analysis on the given multi-omics dataset.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- the multi-omics dataset object that is created by the \fBmo_layers\fR function.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneSet\fB \fR\- 
 the gene set collection, it could be a GSEA [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model, a GMT file
 path or other data that could be cast into the background model.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBopts\fB \fR\- the running configuration object that is created by the \fBmogsva_opts\fR function.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [MultiOmicsGsvaResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSVA.MultiOmicsGsvaResult) object which contains the fused pathway activity
 matrix, the per-omics scores, the pathway weights, the omics contribution decomposition
 and the permutation test p-value table (when \fBpermutations\fR is greater than zero).
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The scoring of each omics layer is performed independently (the kernel density
 estimation never mixes the features from the different omics), then the omics specific
 enrichment scores are fused by the configured weight strategy.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GSVA
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
